WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/driving/components/drivetrain-health/PowerOutputChart.tsx (93 lines) — a Recharts
  `AreaChart` inside `<FadeIn delay={0.3}><ChartContainer>`:
    • props: `data: ChartDataPoint[]` (date, powerMax, powerMin, outsideTemp, distance).
    • `if (data.length <= 1) return null;`  → render nothing for ≤1 point.
    • two overlaid <Area>: powerMax (Peak, stroke #8b5cf6 violet, fill dtPwrMaxGrad)
                           powerMin (Regen, stroke #ef4444 red,   fill dtPwrMinGrad).
    • ReferenceLine y={0}; XAxis dataKey="date"; YAxis label "kW".
    • Tooltip = <ChartTooltip/>; legend = <ChartLegend state={hidden}/> where
      hidden = useHiddenSeries('drivetrain-power-output')  → URL-persisted per-series hide toggle.
    • ChartContainer dataColumns (the export menu): Date / Peak (kW) / Regen (kW).
  Upstream (DrivetrainHealthPage): chartData = drives.sort(asc).slice(-30).map(d => ({
      date: formatDateShort(startTs), powerMax: (avgPowerW ?? 0)/1000, powerMin: 0, ... }))
  ⇒ the SI-canonical source is avgPowerW (watts); kW is a /1000 DISPLAY conversion.

